dax: copy no edges of a page onto itself

A filesystem whose copy-on-write moves where its entries map a page,
rather than its data, as Fxfs's DAX does for a page moved to new
blocks it already holds, returns IOMAP_F_SHARED with a srcmap at the
iomap's own address, for the kernel to replace its entries of the
page. dax_iomap_copy_around then copied the page's edges onto
themselves: a store racing the copy, through another mapping of the
page, to bytes the write didn't cover, was undone. Copy nothing when
the source is the destination.

diff --git a/fs/dax.c b/fs/dax.c
--- a/fs/dax.c
+++ b/fs/dax.c
@@ -1318,6 +1318,14 @@ static int dax_iomap_copy_around(loff_t pos, uint64_t length, size_t align_size,
 		ret = dax_iomap_direct_access(srcmap, pos, size, &saddr, NULL);
 		if (ret)
 			return dax_mem2blk_err(ret);
+		/*
+		 * A source that is the destination holds the data already, as a
+		 * filesystem's whose CoW moves only where its entries map the
+		 * pages: copying it onto itself would undo stores racing the
+		 * copy, through other mappings of the pages.
+		 */
+		if (saddr == daddr)
+			return 0;
 	}
 
 	if (copy_all) {
